# What must not reach the build context, and why.
#
# Note what is NOT here: data/. The `portable` stage in the Dockerfile copies the
# whole 3.81 GiB data tree into the image on purpose, so the tree has to stay in
# the context. BuildKit only transfers the files a COPY actually asks for, so the
# `app` stage - which never copies data/ - does not pay for it.
#
# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Host environments and caches. The .venv in particular holds Windows wheels
# whose DLLs this image exists to escape, so copying it in would be worse than
# useless.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.github/

# Built on the host, never in the image: there is no Node toolchain in here.
web/node_modules/

# A download that was still in flight when the image was built. `src.fetch`
# streams to <name>.part and renames only on success, so baking one in would put
# a truncated raster in the image under a name that looks complete - the failure
# mode the fetcher's temp-file dance exists to prevent.
**/*.part

# Runtime output, not input: the approved brief accumulates as the demo is used,
# and a previous session's approvals showing up in a fresh container would be
# read as this session's work.
data/processed/approved.md

# Exploration, not the deliverable.
notebooks/
